---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import '../../styles/global.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Connect OpenMind to Claude or ChatGPT — OpenMind"
  description="Point Claude Desktop, Claude Code, Cursor, or the ChatGPT desktop app at your local OpenMind server."
>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <section class="pt-28 pb-20 md:pt-36 md:pb-28">
      <div class="container max-w-3xl">

        <!-- Header -->
        <div class="mb-12 fade-in">
          <a href="/guides/" class="text-xs text-text-muted hover:text-text-primary transition-colors">&larr; All Guides</a>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mt-4 mb-2">
            <span class="text-3xl">🖥️</span>
            <div>
              <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-text-primary tracking-tight">Connect to Claude or ChatGPT</h1>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mt-1">
                <span class="text-[10px] font-semibold text-cal-gold uppercase tracking-widest">Step 2</span>
                <span class="text-xs text-text-muted">~3 minutes</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-text-body mt-4">
            OpenMind is an MCP server: a program on your computer that gives an AI app a set of
            tools. You tell the app once where to find it, and from then on you just ask questions.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Prerequisite -->
        <div class="card mb-8 fade-in border-border/50">
          <h3 class="text-text-primary font-semibold mb-2">Before you start</h3>
          <ul class="text-sm text-text-secondary space-y-1">
            <li>- <a href="/guides/bcourses/" class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-text-primary">A bCourses token</a>, and <code class="text-text-secondary">openmind setup</code> already run</li>
            <li>- A <span class="text-text-primary">desktop</span> AI app. The web and mobile versions cannot run a local server &mdash; this has to be a program on the same machine</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Get the config -->
        <div class="card mb-8 fade-in">
          <h3 class="text-text-primary font-semibold mb-3">First, get your config</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-4">
            This prints the exact block for every supported app, with the absolute path already
            filled in. Your token does not appear in it &mdash; it stays in your keychain.
          </p>
          <div class="terminal">
            <div class="terminal-header">
              <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#ff5f57]"></div>
              <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#febc2e]"></div>
              <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#28c840]"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="terminal-body text-[13px]">
              <div><span class="text-text-secondary">$</span> <span class="text-text-primary">openmind mcp</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">

          <!-- Claude Desktop -->
          <div class="card fade-in">
            <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-cal-gold uppercase tracking-widest">Claude Desktop</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-4">
              Open your Claude config file &mdash; Settings &rarr; Developer &rarr; Edit Config will take you
              straight there, or find it at:
            </p>
            <div class="text-xs text-text-muted space-y-1 mb-4 font-mono">
              <div>macOS&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json</div>
              <div>Windows&ensp;%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json</div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-4">Add the <code class="text-text-secondary">openmind</code> entry:</p>
            <div class="terminal">
              <div class="terminal-header">
                <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#ff5f57]"></div>
                <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#febc2e]"></div>
                <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#28c840]"></div>
                <span class="ml-3 text-xs text-text-muted font-sans">claude_desktop_config.json</span>
              </div>
              <div class="terminal-body text-[13px] space-y-0.5">
                <div><span class="text-text-secondary">&#123;</span></div>
                <div>&ensp;<span class="text-cal-gold">"mcpServers"</span><span class="text-text-secondary">: &#123;</span></div>
                <div>&ensp;&ensp;<span class="text-cal-gold">"openmind"</span><span class="text-text-secondary">: &#123;</span></div>
                <div>&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;<span class="text-cal-gold">"command"</span><span class="text-text-secondary">: </span><span class="text-text-primary">"/Users/you/.local/bin/openmind-mcp"</span></div>
                <div>&ensp;&ensp;<span class="text-text-secondary">&#125;</span></div>
                <div>&ensp;<span class="text-text-secondary">&#125;</span></div>
                <div><span class="text-text-secondary">&#125;</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-4">
              Then <span class="text-text-primary">quit Claude completely</span> and reopen it &mdash; closing the
              window is not enough. The path must be absolute; Claude does not inherit your shell's PATH.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Claude Code -->
          <div class="card fade-in">
            <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-cal-gold uppercase tracking-widest">Claude Code</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-4">One command, no file editing:</p>
            <div class="terminal">
              <div class="terminal-header">
                <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#ff5f57]"></div>
                <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#febc2e]"></div>
                <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#28c840]"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="terminal-body text-[13px]">
                <div><span class="text-text-secondary">$</span> <span class="text-text-primary">claude mcp add --scope user openmind -- /Users/you/.local/bin/openmind-mcp</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-4">
              <code class="text-text-secondary">--scope user</code> makes it available in every project.
              Check it with <code class="text-text-secondary">claude mcp list</code>.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Cursor -->
          <div class="card fade-in">
            <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-cal-gold uppercase tracking-widest">Cursor</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
              Add the same JSON block to <code class="text-text-secondary">~/.cursor/mcp.json</code>
              (create the file if it isn't there), then reload Cursor. Settings &rarr; MCP will show
              OpenMind connected with its twelve tools.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- ChatGPT -->
          <div class="card fade-in">
            <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 mb-3">
              <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-cal-gold uppercase tracking-widest">ChatGPT desktop</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
              In the desktop app's settings, add a local &mdash; sometimes labelled STDIO &mdash; MCP server,
              and paste the command <code class="text-text-secondary">openmind mcp</code> printed.
              Local MCP support varies by plan and by app version; if you don't see the option,
              check what your plan includes.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

        <!-- Who can use this -->
        <div class="card mt-8 fade-in border-border/50">
          <h3 class="text-text-primary font-semibold mb-3">Who can use this</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
            OpenMind is for a UC Berkeley student running their own copy on their own machine with
            their own bCourses access token &mdash; which is what personal access tokens are for.
            Your token is never shared, collected, pooled, or sent anywhere except bCourses; there is
            no OpenMind server to send it to, and no OpenMind account exists. If you want a friend to
            use it, they install it themselves and generate their own token. Never hand yours over,
            and never run one instance on someone else&rsquo;s behalf. Canvas asks applications that
            operate <em>on behalf of other people</em> to use OAuth; this one operates only on behalf
            of the person who installed it. The maintainer has raised the token policy with Berkeley
            Research, Teaching, and Learning and will follow whatever guidance comes back.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Verify -->
        <div class="card mt-8 fade-in border-l-2 border-l-cal-gold">
          <h3 class="text-text-primary font-semibold mb-3">Check that it worked</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-4">Ask your app:</p>
          <div class="terminal mb-4">
            <div class="terminal-header">
              <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#ff5f57]"></div>
              <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#febc2e]"></div>
              <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#28c840]"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="terminal-body text-[13px]">
              <div><span class="text-text-muted">You &rarr;</span> <span class="text-text-primary">What's due this week?</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
            You should get your real deadlines with priorities. If the app says it has no such tool,
            restart it &mdash; an AI app only reads its MCP config at launch.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Troubleshooting -->
        <div class="card mt-8 fade-in">
          <h3 class="text-text-primary font-semibold mb-4">If something is off</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-4">
            Run <code class="text-text-secondary">openmind doctor</code> first. It checks your Python
            version, the keychain, whether the token still works, your time zone, whether each course
            is reachable, and the catalog &mdash; and names what to fix.
          </p>
          <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
            <div>
              <div class="text-text-primary font-medium">The app doesn't see any tools</div>
              <div class="text-text-secondary">Restart it completely. Check the path in the config is absolute and that the file exists.</div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="text-text-primary font-medium">"Your bCourses token is invalid or expired"</div>
              <div class="text-text-secondary">Generate a new token in bCourses and run <code class="text-text-secondary">openmind setup</code> again.</div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="text-text-primary font-medium">macOS asks for Keychain access after an upgrade</div>
              <div class="text-text-secondary">Allow it. Upgrading replaces the Python interpreter, so macOS sees a new program asking for the same secret.</div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="text-text-primary font-medium">"OpenMind is not set up yet"</div>
              <div class="text-text-secondary">The server is connected but has no config. Run <code class="text-text-secondary">openmind setup</code>, then restart the app.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="text-center mt-12 fade-in">
          <a href="/guides/" class="btn-secondary">&larr; All Guides</a>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
